       <h1>Alia Bhatt's Eternal Sunshine Productions Launches Five Newcomers with 'Don't Be Shy'</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Alia Bhatt</span> <span>#Eternal Sunshine Productions</span> <span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#New Talent</span></div>
       <p>Fourteen years after making her debut as an actor, Alia Bhatt is now marking a significant full-circle moment in her career by actively backing a new generation of talent. This pivotal step sees her transition into a key role behind the scenes, nurturing upcoming artists through her production banner, Eternal Sunshine Productions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/alia-bhatts-eternal-sunshine-productions-launches-five-newco.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Through this venture, Alia Bhatt, in collaboration with Shaheen Bhatt, along with co-producers Grishma Shah and Vikesh Bhutani, has officially launched five newcomers with the project titled &quot;Don’t Be Shy.&quot; This initiative serves as a crucial platform for these emerging artists, underscoring Bhatt's dedication to fostering fresh faces within the entertainment landscape. It highlights her evolving role from a celebrated performer to a producer deeply invested in the future of cinema.</p><p>The launch of &quot;Don’t Be Shy&quot; represents a strategic expansion in Bhatt's professional journey, signifying her commitment to contributing to the industry's growth and diversity. By backing multiple new talents, she demonstrates a clear vision to create pathways for budding actors, solidifying her influence both on and off screen. This development reinforces her position as a prominent figure, now shaping careers as well as her own.</p><p>What to watch: The upcoming debut of &quot;Don't Be Shy&quot; and the five new talents it introduces.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the provided source summary without any embellishment.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
