       <h1>Boxer Sachin Siwach One Win Away From Medal, Moves To Asian Games Quarter-Finals, Preeti Pawar Bows Out</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Boxing</span> <span>#Asian Games</span> <span>#Sachin Siwach</span> <span>#India Sports</span></div>
       <p>Indian boxer Sachin Siwach has advanced to the quarter-finals of the men's 60kg category at the Asian Games. Competing in Nishio, Japan, Siwach secured his spot with a hard-fought victory over Jordan's Mohammad Adnan Abu Jajeh.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/boxer-sachin-siwach-one-win-away-from-medal-moves-to-asian-g.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The bout saw Siwach deliver a determined performance, ultimately prevailing with a 4-1 decision from the judges. This &quot;scrappy&quot; win underlines his resilience and tactical approach in a competitive environment. His progression to the quarter-finals places him just one victory away from guaranteeing a medal for India at the prestigious continental event.</p><p>Siwach's journey through the tournament continues to build momentum as he navigates the challenging draw. Each win brings him closer to the podium, marking a significant achievement for the Indian contingent. The focus now shifts to his upcoming quarter-final bout, where a win would secure at least a bronze medal.</p><p>Meanwhile, another Indian boxer, Preeti Pawar, has concluded her campaign at the Asian Games. While Siwach moved forward, Pawar's participation in the event has come to an end. The performance of athletes like Siwach is crucial for India's medal aspirations at the Asian Games. His advancement highlights the competitive spirit and talent within the Indian boxing team as the tournament progresses.</p><p>What to watch: Attention now turns to Siwach's quarter-final clash, where a win would secure a medal.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides a factual summary of the source.</p>
