     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-09-25 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Congress Slams Centre Over Bail to Mercenary Matthew VanDyke, Questions Northeast Security</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#National News</span> <span>#Politics</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Security</span></div>
       <p>The Congress party has issued strong criticism against the Centre following the granting of bail to Matthew VanDyke, who has been identified as a mercenary. This development has prompted the opposition party to raise significant questions regarding the state of security in India's Northeast region.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/congress-slams-centre-over-bail-to-mercenary-matthew-vandyke.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>According to Congress, the decision to grant bail to an individual described in such terms raises serious concerns about national security protocols and their implementation. The party's statement specifically linked the incident to the sensitive geopolitical landscape of the Northeast, suggesting potential vulnerabilities or a need for heightened vigilance in that area.</p><p>The criticism highlights a political divergence over the handling of individuals with backgrounds like VanDyke's and their potential impact on national stability. While the specific circumstances of his bail or the details of his activities were not elaborated upon, the Congress's reaction indicates a perceived misstep by the central government.</p><p>This political objection underscores the ongoing scrutiny of governmental decisions pertaining to security matters, particularly in regions considered strategically important. The Congress party's move suggests an effort to hold the Centre accountable for its policies and actions concerning both internal and external security threats, using this specific event as a focal point for broader questions about national safety.</p><p>What to watch: The Centre's official response to these security concerns and the political fallout.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively summarizes the provided source, though it lacks context as the source itself is minimal.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
