       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Mongabay India · 2026-09-25 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Conservation Groups Urge Permanent Halt to Vantara Animal Imports</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Environment</span> <span>#Conservation</span> <span>#Animal Welfare</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>A coalition of 27 global conservation organizations has formally written to Vantara, a private zoo and animal rescue centre in India, demanding a permanent moratorium on the import of wild animals to its facility. This collective appeal comes in direct response to Vantara's earlier announcement of a temporary halt on animal imports, scheduled to last until June 2027.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/conservation-groups-urge-permanent-halt-to-vantara-animal-im.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Vantara, which is owned by India's Ambani family, had previously stated its intention to pause imports for a defined period. However, the international conservation groups are advocating for a more definitive and long-term commitment, calling for an indefinite cessation of all wild animal acquisitions.</p><p>The letter from the organizations underscores concerns within the global wildlife conservation community regarding the practices and implications of private facilities importing wild animals. The call for a permanent ban highlights a desire for more stringent ethical and welfare standards in the management of rescued and captive wildlife.</p><p>What to watch: Vantara's official response to the conservation organizations' letter and the long-term implications for animal welfare policies.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article captures the core facts of the conservationists' letter and the nature of the facility.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://india.mongabay.com/2026/09/ngos-call-for-permanent-moratorium-on-animal-imports-to-vantara/" rel="noopener">Mongabay India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
