       <h1>Dan Lawrence Called Up as Buttler Misses Oval Decider with Hamstring Injury</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#England</span> <span>#ODI</span> <span>#Jos Buttler</span></div>
       <p>England’s One Day International squad has seen a significant change ahead of their crucial series decider, with Dan Lawrence receiving a call-up. This development comes as wicketkeeper-batsman Jos Buttler is set to miss the final match due to a hamstring injury.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/dan-lawrence-called-up-as-buttler-misses-oval-decider-with-h.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Buttler sustained the injury during the second ODI at Headingley, a match that saw the series drawn level at 1-1. His absence is a considerable blow for England, as he is a pivotal figure in both the batting lineup and behind the stumps. The team will now have to navigate the high-stakes decider without one of their key performers.</p><p>The series, currently poised at one win apiece, heads to The Oval for Sunday's final encounter. With the series on the line, the pressure will be immense for both sides. Lawrence's inclusion provides additional batting depth, though it remains to be seen how the team management will adjust the playing XI to cover Buttler's multifaceted role.</p><p>This unexpected change adds another layer of intrigue to an already finely balanced series. England will be keen to secure a series victory on home soil, and the reshuffled squad will need to perform cohesively to achieve that goal.</p><p>What to watch: How England adjusts its lineup and wicket-keeping duties for the decisive match.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate elaboration based strictly on the source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
