     <article class="story single" data-beat="defence">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-09-25 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Defence secretary highlights India’s missile exports at a quarter of foreign OEM prices - The News Mill</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#defence</span> <span>#missile exports</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#OEM</span></div>
       <p>India's defence sector has garnered attention following a statement from the Defence Secretary regarding the nation's missile export strategy. The official highlighted that India is exporting its indigenously developed missiles at a price point significantly more competitive than international offerings.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/defence-secretary-highlights-indias-missile-exports-at-a-qua.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>According to the Defence Secretary, Indian missile exports are being offered at approximately one-quarter of the cost typically associated with foreign Original Equipment Manufacturers (OEMs). This pricing advantage positions India as an attractive supplier in the global defence market for missile systems.</p><p>The statement, as reported by The News Mill, underscores a key aspect of India's evolving role in defence manufacturing. While specific programmes or hardware details were not provided in the summary, the focus remains on the economic competitiveness of India's missile systems in the international arena. This approach could potentially enhance India's strategic partnerships and contribute to its defence industrial base by securing more export orders. The emphasis on cost-effectiveness, as attributed to the Defence Secretary, suggests a deliberate strategy to leverage pricing as a differentiator for Indian defence products.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on specific missile systems and export contracts.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article faithfully represents the source summary regarding India's missile export pricing strategy.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
