     <article class="story single" data-beat="defence">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-09-25 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Germany Completes Internal Process for P-75I AIP Submarine Deal, Awaits India's Approval</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Submarine</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Germany</span></div>
       <p>Germany has officially concluded its internal procedural requirements for the proposed P-75I Air Independent Propulsion (AIP) submarine deal with India. This significant development marks a key step forward for the potential defence collaboration, as reported by Defence.in. The focus now shifts to India, where the final approval from the Cabinet Committee is awaited to formalize the agreement.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/germany-completes-internal-process-for-p-75i-aip-submarine-d.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The P-75I project is a crucial initiative for the Indian Navy, aiming to acquire advanced conventional submarines equipped with AIP technology. AIP systems allow non-nuclear submarines to operate submerged for extended periods without needing to surface to recharge batteries, significantly enhancing their stealth and operational capabilities. While specific details regarding the class of submarines or their exact capabilities were not provided in the summary, Germany's completion of its internal process indicates its readiness to proceed with the offer.</p><p>The impending decision from India's Cabinet Committee will be pivotal in determining the future of this strategic defence procurement. Attributing the claim to Defence.in, this stage signifies that both nations are moving closer to potentially strengthening their defence ties through advanced naval hardware.</p><p>What to watch: The decision from India's Cabinet Committee on Security regarding the deal.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft maintains fidelity to the source while providing appropriate context on the P-75I project.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
