       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-09-25 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Insta360 conquered 360 cameras — now it’s eyeing glasses</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Tech</span> <span>#Cameras</span> <span>#360-degree</span> <span>#Insta360</span></div>
       <p>Insta360, a company whose name directly reflects its primary product, has established itself as the dominant force in the 360-degree camera market. These specialized cameras are renowned for their ability to record every angle simultaneously, offering users the flexibility to capture footage first and then frame their desired perspectives later.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/insta360-conquered-360-cameras-now-its-eyeing-glasses.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While Insta360 did not originate the concept of 360-degree filming, it has successfully become synonymous with the technology. The company's innovative products and strategic market presence have propelled it to an impressive 73 percent of the worldwide market share in the 360-camera category, signifying a near-monopoly in this niche. This strong position underscores its influence and success in consumer and professional imaging.</p><p>Building on its established leadership, Insta360 is now reportedly expanding its ambitions beyond its core camera offerings. The company is actively exploring new product categories, specifically &quot;eyeing glasses&quot; as its next frontier. This strategic pivot suggests a move towards wearable technology or augmented reality devices, leveraging its expertise in capturing immersive visual experiences.</p><p>What to watch: Details regarding Insta360's new glasses product line and its impact on the wearable tech market.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the source, though 'eyeing glasses' is inferred from the source's trailing text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/999489/insta360-smart-glasses-mirrorless-interview" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
