       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-09-25 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Minor Recounts Horror in Delhi Park, Accused Booked Under BNS and POCSO</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Delhi</span> <span>#Crime</span> <span>#POCSO</span> <span>#BNS</span></div>
       <p>In a distressing incident reported from Delhi, a minor has recounted a horrific experience that occurred at Aastha Kunj Park. Authorities have taken swift action, with accused individuals now booked under relevant sections of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) and the Protection of Children from Sexual Offences (POCSO) Act.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/minor-recounts-horror-in-delhi-park-accused-booked-under-bns.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The case involves a serious offense, with the minor providing an account of the events. The booking of the accused under the BNS signifies that the legal framework for criminal offenses is being applied, while the inclusion of the POCSO Act underscores the gravity of the crime given the victim's age and the nature of the allegations. The POCSO Act is specifically designed to protect children from sexual abuse and exploitation, ensuring stringent penalties for offenders.</p><p>Police investigations are underway to gather all necessary evidence and establish the full circumstances surrounding the incident. The legal process is expected to proceed with due diligence, aiming to bring those responsible to justice. Such incidents highlight ongoing concerns regarding safety and security in public spaces, particularly for vulnerable populations.</p><p>What to watch: The progression of the police investigation and subsequent legal proceedings in this sensitive case.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the provided information without adding unverified claims.</p>
