     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-09-25 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Morne Morkel Advocates Opportunities for Young Pacers in West Indies ODI Series</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Morne Morkel</span> <span>#Prasidh Krishna</span></div>
       <p>India's bowling coach, Morne Morkel, has called for greater opportunities for the nation's second-line fast bowlers in the upcoming One Day International (ODI) series against the West Indies. Morkel specifically named Prasidh Krishna and Gurnoor Brar as players who should be given sufficient chances by the team management during the series. This recommendation underscores a strategic approach to developing a broader pool of talent for India's pace attack.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/morne-morkel-advocates-opportunities-for-young-pacers-in-wes.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The call from the bowling coach highlights the importance of exposing emerging fast bowlers to international competition. Providing these players with game time against a touring side like the West Indies could be crucial for their development, allowing them to gain valuable experience and adapt to the pressures of international cricket. Morkel's emphasis on giving them &quot;sufficient opportunities&quot; suggests a desire for sustained exposure rather spacious appearances.</p><p>Developing a strong bench strength in pace bowling is often considered vital for long-term success in all formats of the game. Such an approach ensures that India has a continuous supply of skilled bowlers ready to step up, particularly given the demanding international schedule. The upcoming ODI series against the West Indies presents a timely platform for the team management to implement this strategy, as advocated by the coaching staff.</p><p>What to watch: The selection decisions for the upcoming ODI series against the West Indies.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly interprets the source summary regarding the bowling coach's recommendations.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/morne-morkel-reveals-plan-for-indias-pace-attack-for-2027-world-cup-sends-message-to-prasidh-krishna-gurnoor-brar-12098178#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
