       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-09-25 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Premier League joins call for Fifa reforms</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Football</span> <span>#Premier League</span> <span>#Fifa</span> <span>#Reform</span></div>
       <p>The Premier League has officially joined a growing chorus of major football organizations advocating for significant changes within Fifa, the sport's global governing body. This move sees England's top football division align with three of its prominent European counterparts in demanding &quot;fundamental&quot; reform of how Fifa is currently operated and managed.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/premier-league-joins-call-for-fifa-reforms.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The collective call for reform signals a united front among some of Europe's most influential leagues. Their shared concern centers on the governance structures and operational practices of Fifa, indicating a desire for increased transparency, accountability, and improved leadership within world football. This unified stance from such powerful entities underscores the seriousness of the issues at hand.</p><p>By adding its voice to the initiative, the Premier League, known for its global reach and financial clout, amplifies the pressure on Fifa to address existing concerns and implement meaningful changes. The specific nature of the &quot;fundamental&quot; reforms sought by these leagues suggests a desire for deep-seated alterations rather than superficial adjustments to Fifa's constitution and day-to-day running.</p><p>What to watch: How Fifa responds to this unified call for fundamental reforms from major European football leagues.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the essence of the source summary provided.</p>
