       <h1>Sharon Levy Departs Endemol Shine North America After Nearly a Decade</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Media Industry</span> <span>#Endemol Shine</span> <span>#Banijay</span></div>
       <p>Sharon Levy is exiting her role as CEO of Banijay’s Endemol Shine North America, concluding a tenure of nearly a decade with the company. Her departure comes amid a significant restructure following a major industry merger.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/sharon-levy-departs-endemol-shine-north-america-after-nearly.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The restructure is a direct consequence of the $8 billion merger between Banijay and All3Media, which finalized this summer. This consolidation has led to changes in leadership and operational oversight within the combined entity.</p><p>Ben Samek, currently the CEO of Banijay Americas, will now assume oversight of the unified U.S. operations for the merged company. This move centralizes leadership for the North American branch under a single executive.</p><p>Levy had been a prominent figure at Endemol Shine North America, rising to the position of CEO. Her exit signifies a new chapter for the production giant as it integrates its operations post-merger.</p><p>What to watch: The strategic direction of the combined Banijay and All3Media U.S. entity under Ben Samek.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is a faithful and concise summary of the provided text.</p>
