     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-09-25 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Student Death at Marwadi University Marks Second Incident in a Week</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#education</span> <span>#campus safety</span> <span>#student welfare</span> <span>#Rajkot</span></div>
       <p>A third-year computer science student from Andhra Pradesh reportedly died by suicide at Marwadi University in Rajkot. The incident, which has drawn attention to student welfare, occurred just a week after another student at the same institution died in a similar manner. This marks the second such tragic event on the campus within a short span.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/student-death-at-marwadi-university-marks-second-incident-in.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The university, located in Rajkot, Gujarat, is now grappling with the implications of these successive incidents. While specific details regarding the circumstances leading to the student's death remain undisclosed in the immediate aftermath, the repeated nature of these events within a single week raises concerns for the campus community and authorities.</p><p>The student, who was pursuing a computer science degree, hailed from Andhra Pradesh, a state in southern India. The incident underscores the broader challenges related to mental health support and student well-being within educational institutions. The proximity of these two events will likely prompt closer examination of the support systems available to students.</p><p>Authorities are expected to conduct further inquiries into the incidents. The university administration faces the task of addressing the underlying issues that may contribute to such tragic outcomes among its student body.</p><p>What to watch: Further university statements and any official investigations into the incidents.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source summary without adding extraneous or unverified information.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/marwadi-university-student-dies-by-suicide-in-rajkot-second-such-case-in-a-week-10353322.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
