     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-09-25 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Union Minister Flags Concern Over Speaking Time for SC/ST MPs in Parliament</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Parliament</span> <span>#Politics</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#SC/ST</span></div>
       <p>Union Minister Jitan Ram Manjhi has voiced concerns regarding the allocation of speaking time for Members of Parliament from Scheduled Castes (SC) and Scheduled Tribes (ST) in the Lok Sabha. The leader of the Hindustani Awam Morcha (Secular), an ally within the National Democratic Alliance (NDA), formally conveyed this issue in a letter addressed to Lok Sabha Speaker Om Birla.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-25/union-minister-flags-concern-over-speaking-time-for-scst-mps.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The matter gained prominence after a BJP MP first raised the concern during a meeting of NDA parliamentarians. Mr. Manjhi's subsequent letter to the Speaker elevates the issue, suggesting a broader sentiment within segments of the ruling coalition regarding equitable participation in legislative debates.</p><p>The communication points to a perceived disparity, advocating for more opportunities for SC and ST representatives to articulate their perspectives and effectively represent their constituencies. This highlights the importance of ensuring that diverse voices are adequately heard within the parliamentary framework.</p><p>This development signals ongoing internal discussions within the NDA concerning the operational aspects of parliamentary sessions. Addressing such issues is considered vital for upholding principles of inclusivity and fair representation in the nation's highest legislative body. The letter seeks a review of existing practices to ensure all members have sufficient time to contribute.</p><p>What to watch: The Speaker's response to the letter and any potential adjustments in parliamentary procedures.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the provided source summary without any embellishment.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/scst-mps-not-given-enough-time-to-speak-in-parliament-says-nda-ally-and-minister-jitan-ram-manjhi/article71509412.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
